PixelU-Wii: copyright and licences
===================================

PixelU-Wii (PixelU\wii\PixelU-Wii.exe) is RetroPixels' GameCube and Wii
engine. This file says who owns which parts of it and under which terms each
part is shipped. The licence texts are in the Licenses folder next to this
file; license.txt is the GNU GPL version 2.


1. RetroPixels' original code and art
-------------------------------------

Every source file that starts with the line

    Original code for RetroPixels (PixelU-Wii). Not derived from Dolphin.

was written for RetroPixels from scratch and is RetroPixels' work. So are
the program icon, the pictures in Sys\Resources (except the font files) and
the Windows dark style, all drawn by pixelu/wii/art/make_art.py.

No licence has been chosen for RetroPixels' original code yet. This notice
does not grant one and does not choose one.

The program as a whole: while PixelU-Wii.exe still contains Dolphin code
(section 2) and is linked with GPL-licensed components (section 4), the
executable is a work based on Dolphin and is distributed under the terms of
the GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any later
version (license.txt, Licenses\GPL-2.0-or-later.txt). The source code is at
https://github.com/shredder565/retropixels (folder pixelu/wii).


2. Dolphin code that is still in PixelU-Wii
-------------------------------------------

PixelU-Wii started as Dolphin 2609a (https://dolphin-emu.org/,
https://github.com/dolphin-emu/dolphin) and is being rewritten one file at a
time (docs/pixelu-wii-original.md lists what is left). Source files without
the line above are Dolphin's, Copyright Dolphin Emulator Project, and keep
the licence named in their SPDX-License-Identifier line: mostly
GPL-2.0-or-later, a few MIT, BSD-3-Clause or CC0-1.0 (Licenses folder).
The build system and Externals glue still come from Dolphin's tree at 2609a
(GPL-2.0-or-later).


3. Dolphin community data, shipped unchanged
--------------------------------------------

These are Dolphin community data (GPL-2.0-or-later), shipped unchanged:

  Sys\GameSettings\          per-game settings and patches
  Sys\ApprovedInis.json      hashes of those settings for RetroAchievements
                             hardcore mode
  Languages\                 translations of the program's texts (compiled
                             from Dolphin's Languages/po)

The rest of Sys, apart from Sys\Resources, also still comes from Dolphin
2609a unchanged and is under the same terms (GPL-2.0-or-later, Copyright
Dolphin Emulator Project): Sys\Themes, Sys\Shaders, Sys\Load, Sys\Profiles,
Sys\Wii, Sys\GC (including the free replacement DSP ROM and the IPL fonts
Dolphin generated from Droid Sans, Apache-2.0), Sys\totaldb.dsy and
Sys\codehandler.bin (Gecko code handler, based on Gecko OS / kenobi's
handler). The game title lists Sys\wiitdb-*.txt and Sys\triforcetdb-en.txt
are GameTDB data (https://www.gametdb.com/) as distributed with Dolphin.


4. Third-party components
-------------------------

PixelU-Wii includes or links the following projects. Each keeps its own
licence and copyright. The standard licence texts are in Licenses\; each
project's own licence file, with its copyright lines, is copied at build
time into Licenses\Externals\<project>\.

  Component                            Licence (Licenses\...)
  -----------------------------------  ----------------------------------------
  Qt 6 (Qt6*.dll, QtPlugins)           LGPL-3.0-only (LGPL-3.0-only.txt,
                                       GPL-3.0-only.txt)
  FFmpeg (avcodec, avformat, avutil,   LGPL-2.1-or-later (LGPL-2.1-or-later.txt)
   swresample, swscale DLLs)
  SDL 3                                Zlib
